   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi there, <div><br></div><div>I am attempting to run a multi-group CFA with imputed data by using the cfa.mi function, but I get the following error:</div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.8px\"><b>Error in colMeans(do.call(rbind, coefList)) : </b></div><div style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.8px\"><b>  &#39;x&#39; must be an array of at least two dimensions</b></div></div><div style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.8px\"><b><br></b></div><div style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.8px\">This is my syntax for the imputation and subsequent CFA: </div><div style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.8px\"><br></div><div style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.8px\"><div style=\"font-size:12.8px\"><div>astra_imput = mice(astra1[ , -c(1, 6, 8, 10, 11, 12)], m=10, seed = 500)</div><div>summary(astra_imput)</div><div><br></div><div>mice.imp = NULL</div><div>for(i in 1:10) {mice.imp[[i]] &lt;- complete(astra_imput, action = i, inc = FALSE)}</div><div><br></div><div>#model</div><div>model = &#39;ASmom =~ fm21ags.1_r + fm22ags.1_r + fm23ags.1_r + fm24ags.1_r + fm25ags.1_r + fm26ags.1_r + fm27ags.1_r + fm28ags.1_r + fm29ags.1_r + fm30ags.1_r&#39;</div></div><div style=\"font-size:12.8px\"><br></div><div style=\"font-size:12.8px\">#cfa with imputed data</div><div style=\"font-size:12.8px\"><div>allgroups.fit = cfa.mi(model, data = mice.imp, meanstructure = TRUE, parameterization = &quot;theta&quot;, estimator=&quot;wlsmv&quot;, ordered = c(</div><div>  &quot;fm21ags.1_r&quot; , &quot;fm22ags.1_r&quot; , &quot;fm23ags.1_r&quot; , &quot;fm24ags.1_r&quot;,</div><div>  &quot;fm25ags.1_r&quot; , &quot;fm26ags.1_r&quot;, &quot;fm27ags.1_r&quot; , &quot;fm28ags.1_r&quot;,</div><div>  &quot;fm29ags.1_r&quot; , &quot;fm30ags.1_r&quot;))</div><div><i><br></i></div><div>Any ideas on where this error might be coming from?</div></div></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
